  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Three students <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">S</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> perform an experiment for determining the acceleration due to gravity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> using a simple pendulum. They use different lengths of pendulum and record time for different number of oscillations. The observations are as shown in the table.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Student No.</td>\t\t\t<td>Length of pendulum<br />\t\t\t<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>)</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Number of oscillations<br />\t\t\t<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Total time for<br />\t\t\t<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> oscillations</td>\t\t\t<td>Time<br />\t\t\tperiod<br />\t\t\t<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>128</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>(Least count of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, least count for time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>)</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are the percentage errors in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> for students <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>, respectively, then the minimum percentage error is obtained by student no&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  },
